# Line-ending and diff rules for this repository.
#
# Goal: the module must load and behave identically under Windows PowerShell 5.1 (Windows only) and
# PowerShell 7.x+ on Windows, Linux, and macOS, no matter what each contributor's core.autocrlf is set to.
#
# Line endings do not affect how PowerShell parses a script (every supported host reads LF and CRLF
# equally), so these rules exist to keep checkouts byte-identical and diffs clean rather than to make the
# code work. Git stores text files with LF internally and applies the eol rules below on checkout.
#
# Every text type is pinned to LF, which is what Git already stores, so a checked-out file is byte for byte
# the repository's copy on every platform and whatever a contributor's core.autocrlf says. That leaves no
# conversion layer to reason about, which matters because Git hides line-ending differences: it normalizes
# before diffing, so a file whose endings are wrong shows no diff and leaves "git status" clean.
#
# CRLF would keep checkouts equally consistent and Windows PowerShell 5.1 reads either, but it reintroduces
# that conversion layer, and every tool here that is not PowerShell (grep, sed, diff, CI, the GitHub web
# view) prefers LF.

# Let Git detect text files and normalize them, unless overridden below.
* text=auto eol=lf

# PowerShell sources.
*.ps1    text eol=lf
*.psm1   text eol=lf
*.psd1   text eol=lf
*.ps1xml text eol=lf
*.psrc   text eol=lf
*.pssc   text eol=lf

# Docs, config, and data. Pinned too, so no text file in the tree depends on core.autocrlf.
*.md     text eol=lf
*.txt    text eol=lf
*.json   text eol=lf
*.yml    text eol=lf
*.yaml   text eol=lf
*.url    text eol=lf
*.csv    text eol=lf
LICENSE  text eol=lf

# Binaries. These must never be line-ending converted or treated as text: the bundled Microsoft WebView2
# assemblies under SKYAPI/Dependencies would be corrupted by any such conversion. Git's auto-detection
# normally catches these, but stating it removes the guesswork.
*.dll    binary
*.exe    binary
*.pdb    binary
*.nupkg  binary
*.zip    binary
*.docx   binary
*.xlsx   binary
*.pdf    binary
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.gif    binary
*.ico    binary
*.snk    binary
*.pfx    binary
*.cer    binary
